title: Aruba Central: Collector Status
agents: linux, windows
author: Kuhn & Rueß GmbH <info@kuhn-ruess.de>
license: GPL
distribution: none
description:
 Monitors the summary lines the Aruba Central CLI prints next to its JSON
 output, for example {Counts: ap: 393 (386:7), clients: 242} and
 {API Rate Limit: 11964 of 11970 remaining}.

 The service runs on the host the agent plug-in {aruba_central} is
 deployed to, not on the access points. The number of access points, the
 clients and the remaining API calls are part of the summary. It is CRIT when the number of
 access points that are down exceeds the levels, and it warns before the
 daily API rate limit of Aruba Central is used up, because no fresh data
 arrives once the limit is reached.

 If the plug-in cannot find any JSON in the output of cencli, the check
 is CRIT and reports the error together with the last lines cencli wrote.
 The details also show which cencli was called and which user the plug-in
 ran as, which is what usually goes wrong on Windows.

 When the section arrives empty, the plug-in was aborted or it crashed -
 on Windows this is normally the runtime of the call exceeding the
 timeout of the plug-in. The check is CRIT in that case as well instead
 of the service disappearing.

perfdata:
 Four values: access points up, access points down, wireless clients and
 the remaining API calls.

inventory:
 One service per host that runs the agent plug-in.
